<title>ITALY: ALPINE SKIING-MEN'S DOWNHILL TRAINING TIMES.</title>
<headline>ALPINE SKIING-MEN'S DOWNHILL TRAINING TIMES.</headline>
<dateline>SESTRIERE, Italy 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leading times in a</p>
<p>downhill training session for those not competing in the men's</p>
<p>combined event at the Alpine skiing world championships on</p>
<p>Thursday (2.9 km, vertical drop 800 metres):</p>
<p> 1. Kristian Ghedina (Italy)   1 minute 37.83 seconds</p>
<p> 2. Franco Cavegn (Switzerland)	 1:38.26</p>
<p> 3. Patrick Ortlieb (Austria)	   1:38.31</p>
<p> 4. A.J. Kitt (U.S.)			1:38.69</p>
<p> 5. William Besse (Switzerland)	 1:39.24</p>
<p> 6. Pietro Vitalini (Italy)	     1:39.29</p>
<p> 7. Cary Mullen (Canada)		  1:39.39</p>
<p> 8. Andreas Schifferer (Austria)	1:39.67</p>
<p> 9. Urs Lehmann (Switzerland)	   1:39.73</p>
<p> 10.Graham Bell (Britain)		 1:39.90</p>
</text>
